Subject: CADStat removeMenu
Message-ID: <7f1cf2c60806181116i28cd9f4et4da0faf3d4ac3bd2@mail.gmail.com>

For the CADStat package on rforge.net we've developed a jgr.removeMenu()
function similar to the jgr.addMenu() function in JGR to allow the JGR menus
to be customized. When CADStat is loaded it removes some of the standard JGR
menus and rebuilds/customizes the menus based on a menu XML file (located in
CADStat/menu/menu.xml).  This allows the menus to be controled via R rather
than Java.

I'd be interested in any thoughts on this approach.

Tom

